      "content": "It's understandable why you feel that way when the weight of your actions is so heavy. That feeling of being fundamentally broken is a very common, yet very painful, experience when we are struggling with intense guilt. The idea of being a mistake is a narrative your mind is telling you, but it is not a permanent fact of your worth. Focus instead on accepting the reality of what happened, not on the impossible task of erasing it.",
